kunyomi.meaning:
a point, a dot. This is used in 2 ways;
a) a dot like the decimal point. . . .actually the 4 dots at the bottom of this kanji are referred to as tens.
b) a point of conversation, as in "That's not the point and you know it!"

mnemonic:
The tree radical has an extra line in it, which I assume makes it the King Tree for being so bad-ass.
Thus;
The bamboo, though humble, is descended directly from the King Tree, since long ago. And it has the family register to prove it!

